WEBVTT

00:46.546 --> 00:48.423
Look at the cake. It's so pretty.

00:50.091 --> 00:52.135
- I guess he's proposing to her.
- I guess so.

00:55.221 --> 00:56.139
It's so pretty.

01:04.898 --> 01:05.899
Hey.

01:06.608 --> 01:08.485
Hey. You got the wrong table.

01:09.069 --> 01:10.236
- No?
- No.

01:10.320 --> 01:11.321
Over here.

01:14.991 --> 01:15.950
I'm sorry.

01:20.497 --> 01:22.749
I'm sorry.

01:22.832 --> 01:26.377
- It's so pretty.
- I'm jealous.

01:26.461 --> 01:28.838
- I guess it's them.
- What's this?

01:28.922 --> 01:30.131
- Goodness.
- I'm sorry.

01:30.215 --> 01:32.550
- It's so pretty.
- I'm jealous.

01:33.218 --> 01:35.804
- That's pretty.
- What's this?

01:35.887 --> 01:38.723
Soo-jin, will you marry me?

01:40.600 --> 01:42.185
Say yes.

01:42.268 --> 01:45.647
- Say yes.
- Say yes.

01:45.730 --> 01:49.234
For me, marriage was a natural thing
to do when the time came.

01:50.109 --> 01:52.779
Like how flowers bloom in spring

01:52.862 --> 01:55.740
and how the rainy season brings
a downpour of rain in summer,

01:56.366 --> 01:58.868
it was in the course of nature.

01:58.952 --> 02:01.162
With the rainy season approaching,

02:01.246 --> 02:03.206
the sweltering heat is in full swing.

02:03.289 --> 02:05.041
It will continue to be hot

02:05.125 --> 02:07.252
until the weekend
when the rainy season begins.

02:07.335 --> 02:09.379
However, as the climate is changing

02:09.462 --> 02:12.799
and the uncertainty
of weather forecasting is increasing…

02:12.882 --> 02:14.175
He's so cool.

02:14.259 --> 02:15.635
Why is he taking such a risk?

02:15.718 --> 02:16.636
What?

02:16.719 --> 02:18.638
- I'm jealous.
- He's really cool.

02:19.264 --> 02:21.891
Well, it's too noisy here.

02:21.975 --> 02:23.434
Should we go now?

02:24.394 --> 02:25.228
Okay.

02:27.772 --> 02:32.068
Is there anything
that we can take for granted?

02:32.569 --> 02:33.945
No way.

02:34.821 --> 02:36.531
How is it possible?

02:36.614 --> 02:38.908
They're dating?

02:39.409 --> 02:41.244
You must be mistaken.

02:41.327 --> 02:43.037
I saw them with my own eyes.

02:43.121 --> 02:46.166
I saw Ha-kyung and Si-woo
eating and drinking together.

02:46.249 --> 02:47.667
They're on the same team.

02:47.750 --> 02:49.252
So isn't that normal?

02:49.335 --> 02:52.630
And Ha-kyung isn't Si-woo's type.

02:52.714 --> 02:53.923
He isn't her type either.

02:54.007 --> 02:56.759
She'd never like anyone
so haughty and reckless.

02:56.843 --> 02:58.261
Exactly.

02:58.344 --> 03:00.847
The two of them dating is nonsense.

03:02.682 --> 03:04.392
Jeez.

03:14.777 --> 03:16.446
I'm sure

03:16.529 --> 03:18.990
Si-woo approached Ha-kyung
to get back at me.

03:19.073 --> 03:20.617
What are you saying?

03:21.200 --> 03:24.579
Si-woo oppa is unpredictable,
but he'd never do that.

03:26.414 --> 03:27.498
"Oppa"?

03:28.291 --> 03:30.251
Did you just call him oppa?

03:32.378 --> 03:34.422
I take it back. It was my mistake.

03:35.298 --> 03:37.133
Anyway, he isn't that kind of person.

03:38.468 --> 03:41.638
I see. If he isn't,

03:41.721 --> 03:43.348
why did he do this to my face?

03:43.431 --> 03:46.100
- That's because you--
- Hey.

03:46.601 --> 03:48.353
Don't side with that jerk.

03:51.481 --> 03:52.732
What?

03:52.815 --> 03:54.192
Do you have something to say?

03:57.195 --> 03:59.405
Anyway, they aren't together.

04:00.114 --> 04:03.326
So don't drag other people
into our problem.

04:04.661 --> 04:07.580
I'm telling you, it's true.

04:08.206 --> 04:09.749
He's trying to get back at me!

04:17.882 --> 04:19.050
By the way, earlier--

04:19.133 --> 04:21.552
What do you want to do on the weekend?

04:21.636 --> 04:23.596
- What?
- It's our weekend off.

04:23.680 --> 04:25.139
Do you want to do anything?

04:25.723 --> 04:27.850
Well, I don't know.

04:30.144 --> 04:31.646
Do you want to see a movie?

04:31.729 --> 04:33.982
The new horror movie
that's coming out looks good.

04:35.149 --> 04:36.109
All right.

04:37.568 --> 04:39.570
We can go for a drive too.

04:40.238 --> 04:41.656
That sounds good too.

04:41.739 --> 04:43.950
Or we can work out together.

04:44.033 --> 04:45.785
You run, don't you?

04:46.286 --> 04:47.287
That sounds good too.

04:49.205 --> 04:52.875
Or we can just go grocery shopping.

04:53.501 --> 04:54.335
Sure.

04:55.753 --> 04:58.006
Why do you say yes to everything?

04:58.923 --> 05:01.092
- What?
- You sound so unenthusiastic.

05:01.759 --> 05:04.887
You said yes to all my suggestions.

05:04.971 --> 05:07.348
I'm really okay with anything.

05:08.641 --> 05:10.643
Actually, I'm happy just walking with you.

05:11.227 --> 05:13.062
I am too,

05:13.646 --> 05:16.691
but let's do something special
on the weekend.

05:16.774 --> 05:18.484
What do you want to do?

05:19.068 --> 05:20.570
Well…

05:20.653 --> 05:22.488
there are so many things I want to do.

05:22.572 --> 05:25.575
I want to go to
the glow-in-the-dark bowling alley.

05:25.658 --> 05:27.827
I want to go on a trip to Jeju--

05:28.328 --> 05:31.039
No, too many people go there
for their honeymoon,

05:31.122 --> 05:32.123
so I'll pass.

05:32.832 --> 05:34.083
What's wrong with that?

05:34.709 --> 05:37.712
Doesn't it feel a little suffocating?

05:38.338 --> 05:39.630
What's suffocating about it?

05:39.714 --> 05:41.632
"The end of love is marriage."

05:41.716 --> 05:44.052
Such an obvious conclusion
isn't the only answer.

05:44.135 --> 05:47.597
But the honeymooners act like
they're the ones who got the right answer.

05:51.267 --> 05:53.061
Not everyone is like that,

05:53.644 --> 05:55.897
but it looks a bit suffocating.

05:59.442 --> 06:01.444
Stay here. I'll get something to drink.

06:01.527 --> 06:03.613
- Okay.
- Okay.

06:14.832 --> 06:20.421
EPISODE 9
DRY CHANGMA (RAINY SEASON)

06:20.505 --> 06:23.174
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

06:26.052 --> 06:29.180
A stationary front has formed
on the southern coast of Jeju,

06:29.263 --> 06:32.433
and it's expected to rain starting
from Jeju early tomorrow morning.

06:33.434 --> 06:36.813
The moving speed
of the stationary front is 35km/h,

06:36.896 --> 06:38.564
which aligns with our initial forecast.

06:39.899 --> 06:41.317
- Did you say 35?
- Yes.

06:42.944 --> 06:45.905
At this rate, it'll start to rain

06:45.988 --> 06:49.575
in the metropolitan area tomorrow evening
as we first predicted, right?

06:49.659 --> 06:50.535
Yes, sir.

06:53.204 --> 06:55.248
- What about the press?
- Yes.

06:55.331 --> 06:56.833
Because of the prolonged heatwave,

06:56.916 --> 06:58.835
they're looking forward
to the rainy season.

06:58.918 --> 06:59.877
Is that so?

07:00.628 --> 07:01.879
Okay.

07:01.963 --> 07:05.049
Proceed with the press briefing
as scheduled and let's move on.

07:05.133 --> 07:07.969
Okay. Jeju Office?

07:10.930 --> 07:12.348
All right.

07:12.431 --> 07:13.641
Good work.

07:13.724 --> 07:15.726
- Good work.
- Good work.

07:15.810 --> 07:18.896
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

07:28.990 --> 07:30.158
May I have a word with you?

07:47.800 --> 07:49.177
Are you dating Lee Si-woo?

07:51.179 --> 07:52.054
What?

07:52.763 --> 07:53.848
What did you say?

07:53.931 --> 07:55.892
I saw you two together.

07:56.767 --> 07:59.520
The restaurant that
I took you to for drinks.

07:59.604 --> 08:01.230
You two were there.

08:03.566 --> 08:05.318
Oh, that day.

08:06.027 --> 08:07.737
Si-woo and I are on the same team.

08:07.820 --> 08:09.405
Can't colleagues drink together?

08:09.489 --> 08:11.032
Did that look like we were dating?

08:11.115 --> 08:11.991
No.

08:12.492 --> 08:15.119
You two kissing made it
look like you were dating.

08:16.746 --> 08:18.122
You're crazy.

08:18.206 --> 08:20.958
Ha-kyung, you've changed so much.

08:21.626 --> 08:24.754
When you were with me,
you hated public displays of affection.

08:24.837 --> 08:27.381
But you kissed him openly at a restaurant.

08:30.718 --> 08:33.846
I knew there was something

08:34.472 --> 08:36.474
when you two bickered.

08:37.058 --> 08:39.352
I thought it was weird
when you pulled him aside,

08:39.435 --> 08:41.562
so I followed you,
and you were very affectionate.

08:42.438 --> 08:43.397
Hey…

08:43.898 --> 08:46.817
how could I turn a blind eye
when my subordinate got beat up?

08:46.901 --> 08:49.862
By none other than
my nutcase ex-boyfriend?

08:49.946 --> 08:51.280
- "Nutcase"?
- Yes, a nutcase!

08:51.364 --> 08:53.866
I had a terribly shameful
office romance with you.

08:53.950 --> 08:55.868
Why would I do that again? Are you nuts?

08:56.452 --> 08:57.954
- Well, that--
- And…

08:59.497 --> 09:01.666
me kissing someone

09:01.749 --> 09:03.626
is none of your business.

09:03.709 --> 09:04.961
- Hey!
- What?

09:05.962 --> 09:07.171
I'm worried about you.

09:07.922 --> 09:09.632
Men know what men are like.

09:09.715 --> 09:11.467
That punk, Si-woo, is a jerk.

09:12.426 --> 09:15.179
I wasn't going to tell you this,

09:15.263 --> 09:17.682
but do you know what he did at my wedding?

09:18.432 --> 09:21.352
If you were such a good guy,
why did you marry someone else

09:21.435 --> 09:23.980
after mailing out our wedding invitations?

09:24.063 --> 09:27.024
Hey, I couldn't help it because of Yu-jin.

09:27.108 --> 09:29.694
But he's using you to get back at me.

09:29.777 --> 09:32.071
So you're worried about me?

09:32.154 --> 09:33.406
Of course, I am.

09:33.489 --> 09:35.616
No, you're worried about people

09:35.700 --> 09:37.660
talking about you if I date Si-woo.

09:37.743 --> 09:39.120
That's part of the reason too.

09:39.996 --> 09:41.831
Wouldn't you be bothered by it?

09:43.416 --> 09:44.834
- Hey!
- What?

09:44.917 --> 09:46.002
Get lost.

09:51.257 --> 09:53.175
Ha-kyung, you can't date him!

09:53.259 --> 09:55.177
He's not the one for you!

09:56.304 --> 09:59.223
Gosh, she's a half-wit.

10:14.572 --> 10:17.158
He's really trying to get back at me!

10:17.241 --> 10:18.868
Seriously.

10:42.141 --> 10:43.851
You look so happy to have the weekend off.

10:44.435 --> 10:47.730
Of course. I haven't had
the weekend off in so long.

10:47.813 --> 10:48.898
Honestly…

10:48.981 --> 10:51.817
I have no one to hang out with
when I have a weekday off.

10:53.819 --> 10:55.946
I wish I was free on my day off.

10:56.614 --> 11:00.451
When I have a weekend off,
I have to look after my kids all day.

11:00.534 --> 11:03.746
I have to take them out to eat
and on field trips.

11:04.372 --> 11:06.332
Working is more relaxing.

11:06.415 --> 11:07.416
I see.

11:10.836 --> 11:13.381
I think I know
what Senior Forecaster Um is going to do.

11:16.342 --> 11:18.386
What are you doing tomorrow?

11:19.011 --> 11:20.971
I'm going on a date.

11:21.055 --> 11:22.932
I hear there's a good musical.

11:23.015 --> 11:25.309
I love musicals. What's it called?

11:25.393 --> 11:28.562
The title is…

11:28.646 --> 11:31.023
- Emergency.
- "Emergency"?

11:31.107 --> 11:32.400
"Emergency"?

11:32.983 --> 11:34.693
- I've never heard of it.
- Sorry?

11:34.777 --> 11:37.488
It's a small theater musical.

11:37.571 --> 11:39.115
A small theater.

11:40.032 --> 11:41.033
What's wrong?

11:42.368 --> 11:44.078
What about you, Assistant Director Shin?

11:44.161 --> 11:47.248
I don't do anything special on weekends.

11:47.832 --> 11:50.876
I make coffee first thing in the morning.

11:51.419 --> 11:53.879
Ki-jun found out.

11:55.172 --> 11:56.132
How?

11:56.215 --> 11:59.844
- I like smelling coffee in the morning.
- He saw us together in the restaurant.

12:01.387 --> 12:03.764
So what did you tell him?

12:04.557 --> 12:06.350
I told him we weren't dating.

12:10.938 --> 12:14.150
I eat a simple salad for breakfast.

12:14.692 --> 12:18.654
After I work out, I clean the house.

12:18.737 --> 12:21.073
Do you think he'll believe that?

12:21.157 --> 12:22.741
Why don't we just come out?

12:22.825 --> 12:24.910
We have to play innocent.

12:25.494 --> 12:27.329
I eat when the food comes.

12:27.997 --> 12:29.790
After lunch…

12:29.874 --> 12:32.835
Let's not go to Daehangno tomorrow.

12:34.587 --> 12:35.921
Why not?

12:36.005 --> 12:38.591
Ki-jun's favorite
spicy chicken place is there.

12:38.674 --> 12:41.427
He goes there from time to time.
He might be there tomorrow.

12:41.510 --> 12:44.513
Classical pianists have
different brain structures.

12:44.597 --> 12:45.639
Actually…

12:45.723 --> 12:47.558
I had a hard time getting the tickets.

12:47.641 --> 12:50.436
Do you want to run along the Han River?

12:50.519 --> 12:51.645
Even if it's the same piece…

12:51.729 --> 12:54.940
No. For the time being,
outdoor activities are prohibited.

12:56.609 --> 12:58.319
But we can't stay home.

12:58.402 --> 13:01.822
The biggest difference is that
jazz pianists have good reactivity

13:01.906 --> 13:04.158
and classic pianists have accuracy.

13:05.201 --> 13:06.160
It's interesting.

13:06.243 --> 13:10.998
Depending on what genre you specialize in,

13:11.081 --> 13:13.250
the brainwave displays differently.

13:14.084 --> 13:16.420
It can apply to us.

13:16.504 --> 13:20.382
We're all weather forecasters,
but local forecasters…

13:22.801 --> 13:25.971
CONTINUOUS HEATWAVE…
JIN HA-KYUNG?

13:26.055 --> 13:29.141
Do you know who he's dating right now?

13:29.725 --> 13:30.726
Who is he dating?

13:31.310 --> 13:32.394
Jin Ha-kyung.

13:34.939 --> 13:35.940
Nonsense.

13:36.023 --> 13:38.025
- What is?
- What?

13:38.108 --> 13:40.653
- What's nonsense?
- It's nothing.

13:42.363 --> 13:43.989
MOTHER-IN-LAW

14:01.966 --> 14:04.927
Hello, ma'am. How are you?

14:07.471 --> 14:08.514
Pardon?

14:09.807 --> 14:13.644
Oh, I'm sorry. I forgot.

14:14.228 --> 14:15.980
I'll tell Ki-jun.

14:17.481 --> 14:18.607
Yes.

14:19.525 --> 14:21.902
Yes, I'll see you on the weekend.

14:21.986 --> 14:23.153
Okay.

14:38.878 --> 14:39.962
Where are you going?

14:40.045 --> 14:42.339
- I'm going shopping.
- Shopping?

14:53.475 --> 14:54.435
Hi, Tae-kyung.

14:55.227 --> 14:57.688
Mom wants you to come by after work.

14:57.771 --> 14:59.189
I'm busy.

15:02.192 --> 15:05.362
If you don't come,
Mom will go to your place.

15:06.405 --> 15:07.823
- Do whatever--
- Si-woo.

15:07.907 --> 15:09.325
What should we have for dinner?

15:10.034 --> 15:11.410
How about budaejjigae?

15:11.911 --> 15:12.912
Do you know how to make it?

15:12.995 --> 15:15.789
- I'll be right there. Bye.
- Well, I know how to order it.

15:17.541 --> 15:19.627
- That's weird.
- What is it?

15:19.710 --> 15:21.003
She can't come?

15:22.296 --> 15:24.298
- She'll be here.
- What?

15:25.382 --> 15:26.300
Mom.

15:26.383 --> 15:28.093
Will you really have it out with her?

15:28.177 --> 15:29.219
Just give up.

15:29.303 --> 15:31.639
How can I? She's my daughter.

15:35.559 --> 15:37.561
What else should we get?

15:38.687 --> 15:40.439
- Dumplings.
- Dumplings?

15:40.522 --> 15:42.399
- Do we have instant noodles at home?
- Yes.

15:42.483 --> 15:45.945
We're ordering budaejjigae.
What toppings do you want?

15:46.028 --> 15:48.489
I need to go to my mother's.

15:48.572 --> 15:49.823
Enjoy your dinner.

15:50.908 --> 15:51.825
To her mother's?

15:53.410 --> 15:55.454
- Did something happen?
- I don't know.

16:04.546 --> 16:09.093
Where should I go
for the field trip assignment this time?

16:10.886 --> 16:11.971
Where are you?

16:12.054 --> 16:13.847
I'm at work of course.

16:13.931 --> 16:15.724
I told you he left earlier.

16:18.352 --> 16:20.521
Where in the world is he staying?

16:23.357 --> 16:24.233
Mom?

16:25.985 --> 16:26.860
Yes?

16:27.444 --> 16:29.488
Nothing. I'll take care of it.

16:31.156 --> 16:33.158
- What is it?
- A field trip.

16:37.830 --> 16:39.123
I know where to go.

16:42.001 --> 16:44.753
Think of it as your mother's last wish.

16:45.337 --> 16:47.172
Just three blind dates.

16:47.798 --> 16:50.175
Yes, Ha-kyung. Try it.

16:51.760 --> 16:53.137
I told you no.

16:53.220 --> 16:55.431
Will you let my money go to waste?

16:55.514 --> 16:57.850
What about my time that'll go to waste?

16:58.642 --> 17:00.060
So…

17:00.144 --> 17:02.229
just go on only three blind dates.

17:03.564 --> 17:06.400
Who knows? You might find the right one.

17:06.984 --> 17:10.612
They say that people who get married
through matchmaking services

17:10.696 --> 17:14.324
have a lower divorce rate
than those who get married after dating.

17:15.117 --> 17:16.702
Why are you looking at me?

17:17.369 --> 17:18.787
Hot romance?

17:18.871 --> 17:21.331
It's meaningless.

17:21.415 --> 17:24.334
Look at her. She acted like
she couldn't live without him,

17:24.418 --> 17:26.503
but she got divorced within a year.

17:26.587 --> 17:28.672
Why do you have to bring that up?

17:28.756 --> 17:29.965
Jeez!

17:34.470 --> 17:37.473
Don't hold memorial services
for me after I'm dead.

17:37.556 --> 17:40.559
Be good to me while I'm alive, okay?

17:41.685 --> 17:42.770
Okay?

17:52.488 --> 17:55.532
How dare you!

17:56.116 --> 17:58.410
It's your mother's last wish
before she dies.

17:58.494 --> 18:01.830
How can you say no just like that?

18:01.914 --> 18:03.040
How?

18:03.665 --> 18:08.087
My goodness. How can you say no so easily?

18:08.170 --> 18:10.714
Stop forcing me to get married.

18:11.590 --> 18:15.302
My goodness.

18:15.385 --> 18:18.138
- I'm leaving.
- Don't be like that.

18:19.640 --> 18:22.309
She's acting like that
because she's really worried.

18:22.392 --> 18:24.728
We are her only children.

18:25.979 --> 18:28.148
Her elder daughter got divorced,

18:28.232 --> 18:30.484
and her younger daughter
broke off her engagement.

18:30.567 --> 18:34.613
I guess she wants us to have someone
to lean on before she dies.

18:35.531 --> 18:36.907
Just grant her wish.

18:39.827 --> 18:42.621
You guys can get married then.

18:42.704 --> 18:44.123
Hey, don't say that.

18:46.333 --> 18:48.710
Do you know how I feel when Mom does this?

18:49.294 --> 18:51.839
I feel like I'm being driven
to the edge of a cliff.

18:51.922 --> 18:55.092
If she really cares about me,
she shouldn't make me feel like this.

18:57.678 --> 18:59.888
Yes. You're right.

19:01.557 --> 19:04.059
Anyway, I hate feeling like this. Bye.

19:29.126 --> 19:30.169
Mom.

19:32.546 --> 19:34.798
Were you happy
when you were married to Dad?

19:36.341 --> 19:39.094
What kind of stupid question is that?

19:40.179 --> 19:42.472
No marriage is always happy.

19:42.973 --> 19:45.517
There are good times and bad times.

19:46.268 --> 19:49.605
When all is said and done,
two is better than one,

19:49.688 --> 19:51.690
and three is better than two.

19:51.773 --> 19:54.067
My friend Mi-jeong's youngest daughter

19:54.151 --> 19:56.570
said she'd live alone forever.

19:56.653 --> 19:57.487
But look at her.

19:57.571 --> 20:00.449
She's happily married with children.

20:01.200 --> 20:03.202
Her husband has a stable job too.

20:05.412 --> 20:08.665
Your friends' daughters
and Ha-kyung may be different.

20:10.292 --> 20:11.919
Maybe she's better off alone.

20:12.502 --> 20:13.337
What?

20:15.380 --> 20:18.258
It just crossed my mind.

20:20.302 --> 20:23.013
Good night.
You must be tired from being angry.

20:36.610 --> 20:37.736
Hi.

20:39.655 --> 20:40.739
Hi.

20:42.115 --> 20:43.909
Your mom called this afternoon.

20:46.745 --> 20:48.872
She wants to have dinner with us tomorrow.

20:49.498 --> 20:50.874
You can come, right?

20:52.584 --> 20:53.919
Did you go shopping again?

20:55.128 --> 20:57.673
- That's not--
- You're so carefree.

20:57.756 --> 21:00.008
Aren't we on a tight budget
because the rent is so high?

21:01.176 --> 21:04.054
We can take out another loan
to pay for the key money,

21:04.137 --> 21:07.057
but you know we need money
for the moving expenses.

21:07.140 --> 21:10.769
Are you saying that
I'm spending thoughtlessly?

21:11.812 --> 21:12.938
If you aren't

21:13.522 --> 21:15.732
you wouldn't have bought
something that expensive.

21:15.816 --> 21:18.110
- Ki-jun.
- Let's not do this.

21:18.193 --> 21:19.861
I don't want to fight.

21:20.737 --> 21:21.571
I'm washing up.

21:42.801 --> 21:44.344
Did something happen at home?

21:50.475 --> 21:51.727
Kind of.

21:51.810 --> 21:54.146
You don't have to worry though.

21:58.984 --> 22:00.319
If you're tired,

22:00.402 --> 22:03.030
we can just hang out at home tomorrow.

22:09.453 --> 22:11.913
Can you come out to the living room?

22:19.963 --> 22:21.131
Do you want some beer?

22:25.469 --> 22:27.137
No, thank you.

22:27.763 --> 22:28.722
I'm good.

22:42.277 --> 22:45.155
I guess we can't stay home.

22:45.238 --> 22:46.323
Right?

22:46.406 --> 22:48.158
Let's avoid crowded places.

22:50.660 --> 22:52.954
Is there any place that's especially quiet

22:53.622 --> 22:54.915
when it rains?

22:58.418 --> 23:01.046
There is one place.

23:02.089 --> 23:04.508
- Where?
- Do you like nature?

23:05.467 --> 23:06.676
Of course.

23:08.845 --> 23:10.514
Can you stand being uncomfortable?

23:14.518 --> 23:15.977
To a certain extent?

23:16.812 --> 23:17.979
Good then.

23:21.358 --> 23:22.984
Where is he going to take me?

23:46.633 --> 23:49.344
What's wrong with you?

24:16.997 --> 24:18.331
It's your day off, right?

24:18.999 --> 24:20.458
We need to talk.

24:20.542 --> 24:22.878
Come to the brunch café when you wake up.

24:22.961 --> 24:24.171
I'll be waiting for you.

24:26.173 --> 24:27.632
No.

24:47.569 --> 24:48.737
You're here.

24:48.820 --> 24:50.071
Lee Si-woo.

24:50.697 --> 24:52.324
- Hi.
- Shall we go?

24:52.407 --> 24:53.325
What?

24:53.408 --> 24:54.993
"Colleagues"?

24:57.329 --> 24:59.289
I'll catch you red-handed.

25:31.446 --> 25:33.281
Where are they going?

25:41.122 --> 25:42.332
Damn it.

25:50.757 --> 25:52.008
HONEY

25:52.092 --> 25:55.136
Where are you? Did you forget
that we're visiting your mom?

25:55.220 --> 25:58.223
We have to leave before 6 p.m.,
so come home before then.

25:58.306 --> 26:00.183
There's enough time.

26:03.103 --> 26:04.646
The traffic is getting better now.

26:05.313 --> 26:07.691
- Where are we going?
- We're almost there.

26:11.278 --> 26:12.904
I hope you like it.

26:36.469 --> 26:37.804
- Thanks.
- You can go that way.

26:37.887 --> 26:39.264
- Okay.
- Thank you.

26:56.614 --> 26:58.241
Who pooped here…

27:02.495 --> 27:05.373
Jeez.

27:08.710 --> 27:12.297
HONEY

27:19.763 --> 27:20.597
It's really nice.

27:22.849 --> 27:23.975
- Aren't you glad we came?
- Yes.

27:24.059 --> 27:26.519
- Isn't it too heavy?
- No, it's okay.

27:40.283 --> 27:43.119
Why won't he text me back? Where is he?

27:55.715 --> 27:59.511
The person you are trying to reach
is unavailable. Please leave a message…

28:08.395 --> 28:11.147
We have to go to Camping Site B.

28:11.731 --> 28:12.982
We should go that way.

28:13.608 --> 28:15.652
It's a little far.

28:15.735 --> 28:17.278
It's okay. We can walk.

28:17.362 --> 28:18.488
- Let's go.
- Okay.

28:19.864 --> 28:21.241
- Do you need help?
- No.

28:21.324 --> 28:22.826
- Will you be okay?
- Yes.

28:22.909 --> 28:24.327
Let's go.

28:24.411 --> 28:26.496
It looks light. Let me get on.

28:26.579 --> 28:28.832
Are you going to sit there? I'll pull you.

28:28.915 --> 28:31.543
I'll collect evidence
so she can't deny it.

28:36.923 --> 28:37.882
Where's my phone?

28:38.633 --> 28:40.552
There's enough time.

28:44.597 --> 28:47.142
Damn it! Why did I leave it there?

29:33.396 --> 29:34.564
Did she go somewhere?

29:35.857 --> 29:37.776
Si-woo, did you eat?

29:39.736 --> 29:41.654
Should we go out
and grab something to eat?

29:43.907 --> 29:46.826
Jeez. I guess they're both out.

29:49.329 --> 29:50.497
Well…

30:00.298 --> 30:01.800
MOBILE DISASTER PREVENTION
AND WEATHER SYSTEM

30:01.883 --> 30:02.717
NO CONNECTION

30:08.932 --> 30:11.059
That's weird. There's no connection.

30:11.142 --> 30:12.602
The internet isn't working, right?

30:13.186 --> 30:14.020
No.

30:14.103 --> 30:16.272
He said it'd work.

30:16.356 --> 30:18.483
I just want to check
the real-time conditions.

30:20.735 --> 30:21.945
Hold on a second.

30:24.656 --> 30:26.032
- What is it?
- Seok-ho.

30:26.616 --> 30:29.327
Can you check the radar, please?

30:29.911 --> 30:31.621
You can do it yourself.

30:32.997 --> 30:35.333
I'm outside and there's no internet here.

30:36.125 --> 30:37.210
Please do me a favor.

30:41.798 --> 30:43.091
Wait.

30:43.174 --> 30:44.008
What did he say?

30:44.092 --> 30:46.427
He'll check. Give me your phone.

30:47.428 --> 30:49.055
Right now

30:49.138 --> 30:50.890
the stationary front is moving north.

30:50.974 --> 30:54.352
Jeju is getting 5mm of rain
and the South Sea is getting a few drops.

30:54.435 --> 30:55.645
Okay.

30:57.689 --> 31:00.567
Raindrops are falling in Jeju
and the southern regions.

31:03.069 --> 31:04.320
Seok-ho, hold on.

31:04.904 --> 31:07.282
Ask him for the NWP model from 1 p.m. too.

31:07.365 --> 31:08.783
The NWP model too?

31:11.411 --> 31:12.662
Who are you with?

31:16.958 --> 31:18.918
My girlfriend.

31:22.505 --> 31:23.756
Then forget about it

31:24.674 --> 31:25.925
and focus on your date.

31:26.426 --> 31:30.471
Chief Team One will monitor
the real-time situation.

31:30.555 --> 31:31.681
- Bye.
- Okay.

31:36.644 --> 31:37.729
What did he say?

31:38.605 --> 31:41.065
He told me not to worry about it
and do my thing

31:41.149 --> 31:43.776
because there are people
working at the KMA other than me.

31:44.485 --> 31:46.654
I know that. I'm just curious.

31:46.738 --> 31:48.072
Seok-ho is right.

31:48.156 --> 31:50.700
We need to rest
to cheer up and work again.

31:50.783 --> 31:53.828
The stationary front is heading north
as we expected.

31:53.912 --> 31:56.372
So let's forget about it
and focus on each other.

31:57.665 --> 31:58.666
Okay.

32:02.712 --> 32:04.255
- Should I wash these?
- Yes.

32:26.194 --> 32:27.278
Yes.

32:28.321 --> 32:29.364
Yes.

32:29.989 --> 32:31.574
Chief Team One will do a good job.

32:33.159 --> 32:34.160
Yes.

32:43.002 --> 32:45.296
A vanilla latte with soy instead of milk

32:45.380 --> 32:47.423
and add only two syrups please.

32:47.507 --> 32:49.133
I'll use my coupon.

32:49.634 --> 32:52.053
- What's your name?
- It's Shin Seok-ho.

32:57.350 --> 32:58.309
It's not there.

32:59.435 --> 33:01.854
Not there? I got a stamp the other day.

33:02.438 --> 33:04.691
- From me?
- No, from the other clerk.

33:04.774 --> 33:05.817
Okay.

33:06.442 --> 33:07.735
I'm getting coffee.

33:07.819 --> 33:10.697
I'll check it with my boss later.

33:10.780 --> 33:12.156
Can you pay for this for now?

33:12.740 --> 33:15.618
Excuse me. My coupon is gone.

33:15.702 --> 33:17.704
You said you'd keep it safe.

33:17.787 --> 33:18.913
This isn't right.

33:21.207 --> 33:23.376
What? Apartment number 1302?

33:24.919 --> 33:26.421
Other customers are waiting.

33:26.504 --> 33:28.464
Please check again.

33:37.598 --> 33:38.808
Hello.

33:38.891 --> 33:40.852
Hey. What brings you here?

33:42.061 --> 33:43.855
I'm here to get coffee, of course.

33:43.938 --> 33:44.897
Okay.

33:44.981 --> 33:47.608
What's going on, apartment number 1302?

33:48.693 --> 33:51.362
They lost my fully stamped coupon.

33:52.697 --> 33:54.365
Did you leave it with them?

33:54.449 --> 33:57.493
Well, I already told him
that I couldn't find it

33:58.077 --> 33:59.078
at the moment.

33:59.829 --> 34:04.000
I'll check with the manager later,
so if you could pay for it--

34:04.083 --> 34:06.210
I was going to use my coupon,
so I didn't bring my wallet.

34:07.003 --> 34:09.547
- Do you want me to cancel your order?
- Seriously?

34:10.131 --> 34:12.258
- I'll pay for it.
- It's okay.

34:12.341 --> 34:14.510
You helped me last time.

34:15.344 --> 34:16.804
What did you order?

34:18.014 --> 34:20.141
A vanilla latte with soy instead of milk

34:20.224 --> 34:22.226
and two pumps of syrup.

34:23.478 --> 34:26.189
That and one cool, iced Americano please.

34:26.272 --> 34:27.648
I'll pay for them both.

34:27.732 --> 34:28.858
Okay.

34:29.442 --> 34:30.693
Well…

34:31.819 --> 34:34.947
"cool, iced Americano"
is an incorrect expression

34:35.031 --> 34:38.117
because iced means it's already cool.

34:42.455 --> 34:45.291
- Don't you think I know that?
- Right.

34:47.418 --> 34:49.128
- Thank you.
- Sure.

34:58.679 --> 35:00.515
One chamomile, please.

35:10.358 --> 35:12.777
Wait! Sir!

35:12.860 --> 35:14.028
Wait!

35:14.112 --> 35:15.613
My car!

35:15.696 --> 35:18.658
Wait! Wait for me!

35:19.408 --> 35:20.409
Hey!

35:27.959 --> 35:29.252
What?

35:29.836 --> 35:31.379
I can't stop thinking about it.

35:33.089 --> 35:34.298
It'll rain, right?

35:38.010 --> 35:40.096
It will. The sky is so dark.

35:40.721 --> 35:41.889
It'll rain.

35:52.441 --> 35:53.484
Hey.

35:58.322 --> 35:59.448
You're curious too.

36:01.033 --> 36:03.202
Let's do this. Give me your phone.

36:05.997 --> 36:09.542
Whoever picks up their phone first
has to do the dishes.

36:11.335 --> 36:13.004
Okay, then…

36:13.588 --> 36:15.923
don't we need to cook first?

36:16.799 --> 36:19.635
Camping is all about barbecue.

36:19.719 --> 36:21.220
Okay.

36:23.181 --> 36:24.473
What did you bring?

36:25.808 --> 36:26.893
What?

36:31.647 --> 36:32.690
What is it?

36:35.359 --> 36:37.820
I thought I packed meat.

37:12.063 --> 37:13.189
It's okay.

37:13.731 --> 37:15.816
Camping is all about having kimchi stew.

37:15.900 --> 37:17.944
We have nothing to make broth with.

37:19.695 --> 37:21.948
Should I go and get some meat?

37:22.031 --> 37:24.033
It's okay. All we need is kimchi.

37:28.371 --> 37:30.248
It's okay.

37:51.102 --> 37:53.521
How is it coming along?

37:53.604 --> 37:56.357
- Is it good?
- I don't know.

37:56.440 --> 37:57.817
I haven't tasted it yet.

37:57.900 --> 37:59.860
- You're a good cook.
- Try it.

37:59.944 --> 38:01.362
- Can I?
- Yes.

38:05.616 --> 38:06.784
- It's good.
- Is it?

38:06.867 --> 38:07.952
Try it.

38:11.080 --> 38:12.832
- Isn't it good?
- I think I'm a genius.

38:13.416 --> 38:14.792
It's good.

38:14.875 --> 38:16.210
Stay there. Look here.

38:17.670 --> 38:20.881
VEHICLES SUBJECT TO FINES AND TOWS

38:26.929 --> 38:30.057
HONEY

38:30.141 --> 38:32.351
- Hey.
- Where are you?

38:33.644 --> 38:35.980
- Well, Yu-jin…
- I'll go straight to your mother's.

38:36.063 --> 38:37.523
Meet me there, okay?

38:37.606 --> 38:38.816
Don't be late.

39:10.473 --> 39:11.891
Where have you been?

39:13.100 --> 39:14.185
What happened to you?

39:15.936 --> 39:17.563
Something happened.

39:18.981 --> 39:20.733
Did you forget what today is?

39:21.317 --> 39:23.110
It's your mother's birthday.

39:23.194 --> 39:24.278
Hey.

39:25.029 --> 39:27.323
Why do you have to say "your mother"?

39:27.907 --> 39:30.493
You can just call her Mother or Mom.

39:31.077 --> 39:33.913
She called me two days ago
to have dinner with us.

39:34.705 --> 39:36.749
Where have you been all day?

39:36.832 --> 39:38.751
Do you know how awkward it was?

39:40.836 --> 39:42.630
Did Mom say something?

39:43.214 --> 39:45.216
Where have you been?

39:45.299 --> 39:47.676
Do I need your permission
whenever I go somewhere?

39:48.386 --> 39:49.637
There was something

39:49.720 --> 39:52.390
very important that I needed to check.

39:53.724 --> 39:54.892
Don't tell me

39:54.975 --> 39:56.769
you went to see Ha-kyung again.

39:59.105 --> 40:02.400
You said you couldn't believe
that they were together.

40:02.483 --> 40:04.902
Is that so important to you?

40:04.985 --> 40:06.654
You even forgot your mom's birthday.

40:08.906 --> 40:10.241
Why?

40:10.324 --> 40:12.910
When I broke off the engagement
with Ha-kyung and married you,

40:12.993 --> 40:14.620
people said nasty things about me.

40:14.703 --> 40:17.123
They said it was
as if I dumped a faithful wife.

40:17.206 --> 40:20.126
They also called me a two-timer
who made a shameless transfer.

40:20.751 --> 40:23.129
I had to hear all kinds of terrible names.

40:23.212 --> 40:26.173
I can't let Ha-kyung
act like she's a victim.

40:26.257 --> 40:28.717
She's dating none other
than Si-woo, that jerk!

40:28.801 --> 40:29.760
Ki-jun.

40:29.844 --> 40:32.388
I want you to focus on our problem.

40:32.972 --> 40:34.974
There are so many issues to solve.

40:35.057 --> 40:36.600
Exactly.

40:36.684 --> 40:40.646
I need to take care of this
so I can focus on other things, Yu-jin.

40:40.729 --> 40:41.856
So what will you do?

40:43.149 --> 40:44.608
Will you tell everyone?

40:44.692 --> 40:46.235
Why not?

40:47.778 --> 40:49.155
If you do,

40:49.238 --> 40:51.115
people will talk about us too.

40:51.198 --> 40:53.200
Haven't you thought about that?

40:57.621 --> 40:59.039
Be honest.

40:59.123 --> 41:01.500
Stopping her from acting like
a victim is an excuse.

41:01.584 --> 41:04.295
Aren't you just jealous
because they're going out?

41:06.297 --> 41:07.256
Jealous?

41:07.339 --> 41:09.049
Of Si-woo?

41:09.133 --> 41:10.676
Why would I be?

41:10.759 --> 41:12.470
You must know why better than I do.

41:33.115 --> 41:34.325
It's not raining.

41:36.243 --> 41:37.411
It's not.

41:43.918 --> 41:45.377
It doesn't look like it will.

41:48.214 --> 41:49.507
It probably won't.

41:51.091 --> 41:52.301
What time is it?

41:55.429 --> 41:57.681
It's 20:21.

41:59.683 --> 42:00.935
We're doomed.

42:03.646 --> 42:04.939
Cheers.

42:06.440 --> 42:07.441
Cheers.

42:12.571 --> 42:15.616
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

42:38.013 --> 42:40.683
The meeting started ten minutes ago.

42:42.184 --> 42:43.018
Okay.

42:44.144 --> 42:47.523
The NWP model showed that
the stationary front was moving north.

42:48.357 --> 42:50.192
Why isn't it raining?

42:50.276 --> 42:52.611
Due to the abnormal development
of anticyclone over the Okhotsk Sea

42:52.695 --> 42:54.154
and the cold air in the north,

42:54.238 --> 42:56.282
the northward movement
of the stationary front is being delayed.

42:57.866 --> 43:01.745
Isn't that what Senior Forecaster Um was
worried about in the last meeting?

43:03.038 --> 43:04.248
It is.

43:09.003 --> 43:10.713
When will it rain?

43:10.796 --> 43:13.465
We're expecting it
to come early next week.

43:13.549 --> 43:16.176
But if this continues,
the possibility of further delay

43:16.260 --> 43:17.720
can't be ruled out.

43:20.222 --> 43:21.724
Goodness.

43:24.435 --> 43:27.229
First of all,
send explanatory data to the media

43:27.313 --> 43:30.357
about why the rain is delayed.

43:31.025 --> 43:31.942
Let's do our best

43:33.360 --> 43:35.154
to monitor the situation.

43:35.821 --> 43:36.864
- Okay.
- Okay.

43:36.947 --> 43:39.783
Wouldn't it be better to mention
the possibility of dry changma

43:39.867 --> 43:41.285
for the sake of the future?

43:41.869 --> 43:43.704
- "Dry changma"?
- Yes.

43:44.246 --> 43:46.999
We can't do that because
the stationary front is still there.

43:48.167 --> 43:50.544
Even if it is cloudy and there is no rain,

43:50.628 --> 43:52.546
there's a higher chance of precipitation.

43:52.630 --> 43:54.965
So it's wrong
to make a hasty announcement.

44:00.012 --> 44:01.722
Isn't making hasty conclusions
your specialty?

44:02.306 --> 44:03.140
What is it?

44:03.223 --> 44:05.726
Is your hunch not working this time?

44:07.519 --> 44:09.021
Even that hunch

44:09.104 --> 44:12.107
is based on data and meteorological flow.

44:12.191 --> 44:13.901
Either it's right or wrong.

44:13.984 --> 44:15.611
I can't give out vague information

44:15.694 --> 44:18.280
just because
I'm afraid of being criticized.

44:18.364 --> 44:19.907
"Vague information"?

44:19.990 --> 44:23.619
Doesn't "for the sake of the future"
mean "vague information"?

44:27.581 --> 44:29.291
What are they doing?

44:29.375 --> 44:31.418
That's enough.

44:31.502 --> 44:32.920
No. Keep going.

44:33.003 --> 44:33.921
Pardon?

44:34.880 --> 44:36.048
I said keep going.

44:36.548 --> 44:38.926
Why don't you two have a debate about it?

44:39.009 --> 44:40.969
Come up with a conclusion too.

44:41.053 --> 44:44.848
We'll release that conclusion
with explanations to the press.

44:45.432 --> 44:46.600
That'd be good, right?

44:46.684 --> 44:47.935
What?

44:48.727 --> 44:49.937
Is there a problem?

44:51.063 --> 44:53.691
No, there isn't. We'll do that.

44:55.484 --> 44:57.444
Okay. Keep going.

45:13.544 --> 45:14.920
Director Jin.

45:17.047 --> 45:18.465
I'll be back.

45:18.966 --> 45:20.217
Will you be okay?

45:20.926 --> 45:22.010
Yes.

46:00.007 --> 46:02.718
First, let's analyze
why this forecast was wrong.

46:03.927 --> 46:07.347
Aren't we coming up with an explanation
for why the rainy season is delayed?

46:09.475 --> 46:11.435
We need to review starting
from the initial forecast

46:11.518 --> 46:13.562
and see what we missed.

46:13.645 --> 46:17.399
Only then can we explain the gap
between the expected and actual dates.

46:21.445 --> 46:22.321
Okay.

46:22.988 --> 46:24.656
Where should we start?

46:28.285 --> 46:29.703
During the early forecast,

46:29.786 --> 46:32.247
why did you predict
that rain from the stationary front

46:32.331 --> 46:36.752
would fall in Jeju and the southern part
of Korea five days later?

46:37.628 --> 46:41.006
If you look at the strong wind
at 200hPa above the stationary front

46:41.590 --> 46:44.009
and the speed of the anticyclone
of the North Pacific,

46:44.092 --> 46:46.595
there was a possibility of development.

46:51.892 --> 46:53.310
The explanation isn't out yet?

46:53.393 --> 46:54.394
No.

46:59.066 --> 47:00.317
Do you know

47:00.400 --> 47:02.277
why it's being delayed?

47:02.361 --> 47:03.987
I guess they're revising it.

47:13.956 --> 47:15.707
I'm right.

47:16.291 --> 47:17.376
Look at this.

47:17.459 --> 47:19.878
This upper part is strong,
so the lower can't move up.

47:20.462 --> 47:21.338
I'm right.

47:21.421 --> 47:23.507
- It's too weak.
- Mr. Lee, look.

47:23.590 --> 47:27.970
This front isn't able to move up
because of the anticyclone.

47:28.053 --> 47:31.098
That's why it's not happening.
You're missing that.

48:14.808 --> 48:17.894
- Hello.
- Hello.

48:24.276 --> 48:26.361
- Where is Forecaster Lee?
- Well…

48:27.070 --> 48:29.823
he's at the Office of Spokesperson
preparing the explanation.

48:30.407 --> 48:33.744
He said he sent the details
of today's work to your email.

48:34.536 --> 48:36.705
- Here it is.
- Okay.

48:39.958 --> 48:41.793
- Good work.
- Good work.

48:41.877 --> 48:43.003
Good work.

48:43.920 --> 48:45.255
Don't worry.

48:45.339 --> 48:47.591
- Doors closing.
- They won't fight again.

48:50.260 --> 48:51.678
Let's grab dinner.

48:51.762 --> 48:52.929
- Okay.
- Okay.

48:53.513 --> 48:55.974
- I want something refreshing.
- Like what?

48:57.476 --> 48:58.477
Cold noodles.

49:09.780 --> 49:13.200
It was wrong to analyze that
the stationary front was moving north

49:13.283 --> 49:16.662
due to the trough and strong winds
in the central-northern region of China.

49:18.580 --> 49:21.249
Anyone would have made that conclusion.

49:21.958 --> 49:24.961
Senior Forecaster Um's theory
that the stationary front

49:25.045 --> 49:26.838
would move south made sense,

49:26.922 --> 49:28.674
but the probability was low.

49:28.757 --> 49:31.343
You said you trusted your hunch.

49:31.426 --> 49:34.388
But when you had to take responsibility,
you went with probability.

49:35.347 --> 49:37.724
Isn't that a lame excuse?

49:39.559 --> 49:41.061
Because I wasn't sure.

49:43.814 --> 49:45.816
Someone told me that it was too risky

49:46.692 --> 49:49.152
to go with my intuition
because the safety of too many people

49:49.778 --> 49:50.946
was at stake.

50:03.583 --> 50:06.712
Then why are you taking
a risk with Ha-kyung?

50:07.963 --> 50:11.049
She looks strong,
but she's actually tender-hearted.

50:11.133 --> 50:13.844
She must have had
a hard time because I hurt her.

50:13.927 --> 50:15.762
We're working on explanatory data.

50:15.846 --> 50:19.683
If you're dating Ha-kyung
because you're mad at me or my wife…

50:22.018 --> 50:23.770
you should stop seeing her.

50:26.064 --> 50:27.983
Ha-kyung never does anything poorly.

50:28.608 --> 50:32.154
If she really did start something,
then she must be sincere.

50:32.738 --> 50:34.698
So if she gets hurt again,

50:34.781 --> 50:37.659
she might not be able to recuperate.

50:38.952 --> 50:41.997
You're the one who hurt her.

50:42.080 --> 50:43.665
Don't you think you're being too nosy?

50:43.749 --> 50:45.000
Exactly.

50:47.753 --> 50:49.796
Because I hurt her,

50:49.880 --> 50:51.673
I'm worried about her too.

51:01.057 --> 51:02.559
Don't worry.

51:03.185 --> 51:04.895
I'm also the type of person

51:04.978 --> 51:07.522
who doesn't start something
if I'm not sincere about it.

51:19.075 --> 51:20.994
Release this as an explanation.

51:23.830 --> 51:25.207
I'll get going then.

51:29.586 --> 51:31.004
By the way…

51:38.386 --> 51:40.180
See you next week, Seong-jun.

51:40.263 --> 51:41.473
Bye.

52:55.797 --> 52:56.882
Why…

52:58.425 --> 53:00.302
did you break up with him?

53:02.762 --> 53:03.722
What?

53:03.805 --> 53:06.641
Honestly, he seems like a good man.

53:07.475 --> 53:08.643
No…

53:09.394 --> 53:10.812
he is a good man.

53:11.396 --> 53:13.857
Why did you leave him and come to me?

53:17.903 --> 53:19.529
Don't you know?

53:19.613 --> 53:20.780
No.

53:22.991 --> 53:24.576
I really don't.

53:25.201 --> 53:26.953
You asked me to marry you.

53:30.582 --> 53:32.167
You were the first.

53:33.543 --> 53:36.463
You were the first man to ask me

53:36.546 --> 53:39.215
to marry him, not just date.

53:43.678 --> 53:44.971
I'm sorry.

53:46.181 --> 53:47.724
You married

53:47.807 --> 53:49.976
a penniless bloke.

53:53.688 --> 53:55.941
That's why you're not
registering our marriage.

54:00.612 --> 54:02.948
Why are you so pathetic?

54:03.031 --> 54:05.325
Do you think that's why I put off

54:05.408 --> 54:06.952
our marriage registration?

54:07.535 --> 54:08.370
Then why?

54:08.453 --> 54:09.829
Honestly…

54:09.913 --> 54:13.166
you haven't really focused on us
since we got married.

54:13.917 --> 54:17.545
You're worried about
what others think of our marriage.

54:17.629 --> 54:20.382
Now you're so concerned
about Ha-kyung dating Si-woo

54:20.465 --> 54:23.635
that you can't even focus on anything.

54:24.678 --> 54:27.097
How can I register our marriage
when I'm not sure

54:27.180 --> 54:28.598
if you even love me anymore?

54:30.767 --> 54:31.893
How can I trust you?

54:31.977 --> 54:34.062
Don't make excuses.

54:35.397 --> 54:36.690
There's only one reason.

54:36.773 --> 54:40.276
Keep your eyes on me.
You said you loved me.

55:16.563 --> 55:18.356
Did something happen with Ki-jun?

55:20.984 --> 55:22.318
I want to do better.

55:22.402 --> 55:23.987
- What?
- What?

55:24.612 --> 55:26.114
Let's analyze

55:26.990 --> 55:29.701
- the stationary front again.
- Why?

55:30.201 --> 55:31.828
Did you catch a strange signal?

55:31.911 --> 55:35.081
No, I found something when I was
working with Deputy Director Han.

55:35.165 --> 55:36.207
Here.

55:37.333 --> 55:39.377
The Okhotsk air mass,
which has been developing abnormally,

55:39.461 --> 55:41.004
is stopping its expansion.

55:41.087 --> 55:43.214
There's also an inflow
of water vapor from the southwest.

55:43.298 --> 55:45.216
Isn't it still too weak

55:45.300 --> 55:47.761
to activate the anticyclone
of the North Pacific?

55:47.844 --> 55:49.763
- What do you think?
- I agree with you.

55:50.638 --> 55:52.974
Take a look at this part.

55:53.058 --> 55:55.935
Don't you think
the rain particles are getting larger?

55:56.019 --> 55:57.687
It's uncertain.

55:58.480 --> 56:00.565
If the anticyclone over
the Okhotsk Sea stops developing

56:00.648 --> 56:02.859
and water vapor continues
to flow in from the southwest,

56:02.942 --> 56:05.278
the anticyclone of
the North Pacific will expand.

56:05.361 --> 56:07.155
Then I think

56:07.238 --> 56:09.324
it'll definitely rain in two days.

56:21.836 --> 56:24.380
Let's go with
Forecaster Lee's forecast this time.

56:24.464 --> 56:27.008
Because water vapor is flowing in
from the south.

56:28.009 --> 56:30.470
If you say so. Okay.

56:31.513 --> 56:33.515
Thank you for trusting me.

56:39.229 --> 56:41.981
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

57:07.298 --> 57:11.386
THE KMA'S WEATHER FORECAST
IS WRONG AGAIN

57:19.185 --> 57:21.563
THE FORECAST IS WRONG AGAIN
WHAT IS THE PROBLEM?

57:33.241 --> 57:35.493
The KMA's forecast was wrong again.

57:35.577 --> 57:37.495
What's the reason?

57:37.579 --> 57:39.289
As global warming accelerates,

57:39.372 --> 57:41.875
the variables of the prediction,
including natural cycle fluctuations

57:41.958 --> 57:44.586
such as El Niño and La Niña,
have become much more complex.

57:44.669 --> 57:46.504
Can you put it simply?

57:47.172 --> 57:48.465
It's like having to guess

57:48.548 --> 57:51.426
the path of a vehicle
that ignores traffic signals

57:51.509 --> 57:52.927
and driving lines.

57:55.847 --> 57:57.557
The reporters are excited.

57:57.640 --> 58:01.060
Because there haven't been
any events or incidents lately.

58:01.144 --> 58:03.021
Director Jin has been

58:03.104 --> 58:05.732
having a hard time since she got promoted.

58:06.649 --> 58:08.860
Nothing's going her way.

58:25.919 --> 58:27.420
Aren't you tired?

58:30.882 --> 58:31.883
Let's go inside.

58:34.260 --> 58:35.428
I'm sorry.

58:35.512 --> 58:37.555
If I hadn't insisted,

58:39.390 --> 58:40.850
we wouldn't have been wrong.

58:42.644 --> 58:44.395
You weren't wrong.

58:45.104 --> 58:47.315
Senior Forecaster Um
and I weren't right either.

58:48.942 --> 58:52.153
Like you said,
weather is about variability.

58:52.737 --> 58:54.489
A small thing

58:54.572 --> 58:56.616
can change everything.

58:57.575 --> 58:58.785
What should we do now?

59:01.287 --> 59:03.456
We got it wrong, so we have to be scolded.

59:28.398 --> 59:29.566
THE KMA'S ERRONEOUS FORECAST

59:29.649 --> 59:31.401
The KMA predicted that

59:31.484 --> 59:33.945
it would rain 50 to 100mm per hour
in Seoul, Gyeonggi,

59:34.028 --> 59:37.532
and Yeongseo in Gangwon Province,
starting this morning.

59:37.615 --> 59:41.494
However, until now,
most of the regions are only cloudy.

59:41.578 --> 59:43.371
Thankfully, there wasn't a storm

59:43.454 --> 59:45.582
 on the way to work,
but people are tired of the KMA's

59:45.665 --> 59:47.375
- erroneous forecasts.
- Bo-mi.

59:47.458 --> 59:49.961
I have a headache.

59:50.044 --> 59:51.045
Okay.

59:51.588 --> 59:53.298
- The KMA's forecast was wrong again.
- Wait.

59:53.381 --> 59:54.924
What's the reason?

59:57.135 --> 59:58.595
As global warming accelerates,

59:58.678 --> 01:00:01.556
the variables of the prediction,
including natural cycle fluctuations

01:00:01.639 --> 01:00:04.809
such as El Niño and La Niña,
have become much more complex.

01:00:04.892 --> 01:00:06.269
It's like

01:00:06.352 --> 01:00:08.396
having to guess the path of a vehicle

01:00:08.479 --> 01:00:10.732
that ignores traffic signals
and driving lines.

01:00:11.482 --> 01:00:13.026
- It sounds difficult.
- Do you know her?

01:00:13.109 --> 01:00:15.320
- Yes.
- Aren't supercomputers

01:00:15.403 --> 01:00:17.363
with a huge amount of data

01:00:17.447 --> 01:00:19.782
able to predict even such variables?

01:00:22.994 --> 01:00:25.413
Thank you. See you next time.

01:00:36.424 --> 01:00:39.385
You said that the difficulty
of weather forecasting has increased

01:00:39.469 --> 01:00:40.928
due to the rapidly changing climate.

01:00:41.679 --> 01:00:43.640
Shouldn't you come up with a solution?

01:00:44.432 --> 01:00:46.893
So we try to use a lot of NWP model data

01:00:46.976 --> 01:00:49.854
to forecast with more
diverse possibilities in mind.

01:00:51.397 --> 01:00:53.066
So there's no clear solution?

01:00:54.025 --> 01:00:55.693
We'll try harder.

01:00:58.112 --> 01:00:59.364
Trying harder is easy.

01:01:00.573 --> 01:01:02.033
Doing it well is difficult.

01:01:03.868 --> 01:01:04.827
Are we done?

01:01:05.953 --> 01:01:07.914
- Yes.
- Goodbye then.

01:01:10.249 --> 01:01:11.959
I heard you were dating Si-woo.

01:01:15.963 --> 01:01:18.716
Did Ki-jun say that?
I'm sure I told him we weren't.

01:01:20.510 --> 01:01:21.803
He's charming.

01:01:23.137 --> 01:01:24.931
He's innocent, yet smart.

01:01:25.807 --> 01:01:27.684
He has nothing to show for,

01:01:27.767 --> 01:01:29.394
but he has high self-esteem.

01:01:30.645 --> 01:01:32.689
He's really good looking too.

01:01:36.067 --> 01:01:37.694
May I ask you something?

01:01:39.987 --> 01:01:42.115
Why did you break up with him?

01:01:43.241 --> 01:01:46.285
Was it because of his father?

01:01:52.375 --> 01:01:53.793
Do you think you're all that?

01:01:56.129 --> 01:01:57.880
Si-woo's father

01:01:58.631 --> 01:01:59.799
isn't a good man.

01:02:01.551 --> 01:02:04.804
But he wasn't the reason
I broke up with Si-woo.

01:02:06.556 --> 01:02:07.807
Then why…

01:02:09.976 --> 01:02:11.269
Si-woo…

01:02:12.437 --> 01:02:13.771
doesn't believe in marriage.

01:02:16.315 --> 01:02:20.361
He doesn't want to marry anyone.

01:02:33.207 --> 01:02:34.167
By the way,

01:02:34.250 --> 01:02:38.296
Ha-kyung doesn't sincerely date anyone
if they're not a marriage prospect.

01:02:40.298 --> 01:02:42.216
You knew that, right?

01:02:50.933 --> 01:02:52.226
Doors opening.

01:02:53.519 --> 01:02:54.771
Going up.

01:02:58.775 --> 01:03:00.276
Hold on.

01:03:00.359 --> 01:03:01.360
Sure.

01:03:02.361 --> 01:03:03.446
Hello.

01:03:12.455 --> 01:03:14.957
Like how flowers bloom in spring

01:03:15.041 --> 01:03:18.002
and how the rainy season brings
a downpour of rain in summer,

01:03:18.669 --> 01:03:20.087
for me, 

01:03:20.171 --> 01:03:22.632
marriage was a natural thing
to do when the time came.

01:03:24.801 --> 01:03:26.469
As the climate is changing

01:03:26.552 --> 01:03:29.472
and the uncertainty
of weather forecasting is increasing…

01:03:30.223 --> 01:03:31.641
Si-woo…

01:03:32.809 --> 01:03:34.101
doesn't believe in marriage.

01:03:36.646 --> 01:03:40.608
He doesn't want to marry anyone.

01:03:40.691 --> 01:03:44.529
…nothing can be taken for granted.

01:04:25.444 --> 01:04:27.738
I've never thought about a relationship

01:04:27.822 --> 01:04:30.116
that didn't lead to marriage.

01:04:30.199 --> 01:04:32.702
Who are you? My daughter lives here.

01:04:32.785 --> 01:04:33.995
- What?
- Hey.

01:04:34.078 --> 01:04:36.122
You two are living with my daughter?

01:04:36.205 --> 01:04:38.875
Was that man we met in the elevator

01:04:38.958 --> 01:04:40.835
your colleague as well?

01:04:41.460 --> 01:04:42.503
- Thank you.
- Wait.

01:04:42.587 --> 01:04:43.629
Are you the eldest son?

01:04:43.713 --> 01:04:44.672
Why do you ask?

01:04:44.755 --> 01:04:45.840
What's with Yeouido's current temperature?

01:04:45.923 --> 01:04:48.926
Remove the information
from the prevention portal site.

01:04:49.010 --> 01:04:51.304
The incorrect information
on the portal site.

01:04:51.387 --> 01:04:52.972
You told him, didn't you?

01:04:53.055 --> 01:04:56.267
You should have reported it
to me right away!

01:04:57.351 --> 01:05:02.106
Subtitle translation by: Soo-hyun Yang
